---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE, AUTHOR } from "../lib/site.mjs";
---

<Base
  title={null}
  description="Suspicion is not proof. Authority is not proof either. Show me the evidence. A nonfiction book and companion evidence project by Colin Dixon."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="hero measure-lede">
      <p class="eyebrow">Nonfiction · in development</p>
      <h1>{SITE.name}</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Conspiracy, institutional power and the battle over what we are allowed to know —
        written for readers who refuse both blind trust and unfalsifiable belief.
      </p>
      <p class="principle">{SITE.tagline}</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/book">Book overview</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/music">Companion music</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/author">About the author</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/tracker">Evidence tracker (coming)</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="prose measure" aria-labelledby="about-project">
      <h2 id="about-project">The project</h2>
      <p>
        Governments, corporations, intelligence agencies, scientific institutions, media organisations
        and activists have all been wrong at times. Some have lied, withheld evidence or protected
        institutional interest. Conspiracy culture, meanwhile, often turns anomalies into proof and
        treats every contradiction as confirmation.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>The Ministry of Doubt</em> asks how an intelligent person distinguishes genuine conspiracy,
        institutional failure, ordinary incompetence, groupthink, financial incentives, propaganda and
        complete nonsense — without becoming programmable by either side.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="card-grid">
      <a class="card card--link" href="/book">
        <h3>The book</h3>
        <p>Premise, method and the ground the manuscript will cover — without spoilers or draft chapters.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="card card--link author-card" href="/author">
        <img
          class="author-card__photo"
          src={AUTHOR.photo}
          alt={AUTHOR.photoAlt}
          width="128"
          height="128"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <div>
          <h3>{AUTHOR.name}</h3>
          <p>Physics, mathematics and IT background. Australian voice. Builds public evidence tools.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="card card--link" href="/music">
        <h3>Companion music</h3>
        <p>OzeAuMusic singles for the book’s atmosphere — stream on Spotify. Room for a full album of ~20 songs.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="card card--link" href="/tracker">
        <h3>Companion tracker</h3>
        <p>
          A public evidence ledger in the spirit of
          <span style="white-space: nowrap">electiontracker.au</span> — planned to launch with the book.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="note measure-lede">
      This website is the public face of the project. Working files, research dossiers and editorial
      notes are kept offline from this domain on purpose.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
